# Elf

## Lore

The Elves of the Palladium World are tall, handsome, dark-haired and long-lived, with a love of learning, art and magic. One of the archaic races that survived the Age of Chaos and fought the Old Ones, they ruled that world beside the Dwarves for millennia until arrogance and prejudice drove the two into a six-thousand-year war that ravaged both. Their kingdoms are gone; today they live within human society as counselors, mentors and adventurers, grooming humans as heirs to the world they once ruled - though not every Elf is benevolent, and some of Palladium''s most feared sorcerers were Elves.

Elves are scarce on Rifts Earth, oddly so for a race of dimension-travelling sorcerers. The few thousand believed to be there are mostly in Europe and perhaps demon-ridden Asia. With the pointed ears covered, an Elf passes easily for an attractive human.

**Alignment:** Any.

**Size:** 6 feet to 6 feet 10 inches. **Weight:** 100 to 250 pounds.

**Average Life Span:** 600 years.

## GM Notes

Elves are impudent, arrogant and elitist, and also noble, valiant and spirited. Traditional enemies are Dwarves, Gnomes, Ogres, Trolls, Kobolds, Goblins and Hob-Goblins, and they join others against supernatural evil - the Splugorth, the Naruni, Gene-Splicers and the Alien Intelligences above all. Noble Elves get on with Cyber-Knights, Lyn-Srial, True Atlanteans, Chiang-Ku, Psi-Ponies, Fennodi, Faerie Folk, Zembahk and Native Americans, and with scholars, scientists and practitioners of magic generally. Wolfen court their favor and are usually snubbed.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'rifts-elf');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'rifts-elf';

